WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.458 --> 00:00:01.291
(suspenseful music)

00:00:01.291 --> 00:00:03.990
- [Narrator] People in Gaza are
being forced to use seawater

00:00:03.990 --> 00:00:06.510
to clean themselves, wash their clothes,

00:00:06.510 --> 00:00:07.923
and clean the dishes.

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:11.250
This is a result of Israel's siege,

00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:12.780
which restricted the supply

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:15.690
of water, food, fuel, and medicine

00:00:15.690 --> 00:00:17.610
into the Palestinian enclave

00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:20.924
in response to Hamas's
deadly attacks on October 7.

00:00:20.924 --> 00:00:22.080
(refugees speaking foreign language)

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:23.730
- [Narrator] The World
Health Organization said

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:25.489
that more than 2 million Gazans

00:00:25.489 --> 00:00:29.455
have to get by on just three
liters of water per day

00:00:29.455 --> 00:00:32.700
for drinking, cooking, and washing.

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:35.730
That's just 1/5 of the absolute minimum

00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:40.730
of 15 liters needed for basic
survival according to the WHO.

00:00:40.809 --> 00:00:42.630
(pump buzzing)

00:00:42.630 --> 00:00:46.440
Gaza's water crisis began well
before the current conflict

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:48.660
between Israel and Hamas.

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:52.290
Most of Gaza's fresh water
comes from a shallow aquifer,

00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:54.969
which was contaminated
with sewage and seawater

00:00:54.969 --> 00:00:57.450
even before the war.

00:00:57.450 --> 00:01:01.080
The UN has said that as much as 96% of it

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:03.351
is not fit for human consumption,

00:01:03.351 --> 00:01:07.497
so Gazans had to rely on
unregulated private water tankers

00:01:07.497 --> 00:01:10.860
and desalination plants
for drinking water.

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:13.650
There are three major desalination plants,

00:01:13.650 --> 00:01:16.383
while some of the water
is purchased from Israel.

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:18.960
Years of conflicts worsened

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:22.530
the already inadequate
water infrastructure.

00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:27.240
In 2007, Israel and Egypt
imposed a blockade on Gaza

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:31.110
after Hamas took over power in the strip.

00:01:31.110 --> 00:01:34.110
That severely restricted
the entry of materials

00:01:34.110 --> 00:01:36.783
to repair and maintain water systems.

00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:41.280
Then, Israel ordered a total siege of Gaza

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:43.011
after the Hamas attacks.

00:01:43.011 --> 00:01:47.094
(Yoav speaking foreign language)

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:50.850
- [Narrator] In the
aftermath of the assault,

00:01:50.850 --> 00:01:54.074
Israel also turned off water pipelines.

00:01:54.074 --> 00:01:56.850
In late October, Israeli officials said

00:01:56.850 --> 00:02:01.200
that water was flowing through
two of the three pipelines.

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:03.150
As fuel started to run out,

00:02:03.150 --> 00:02:06.090
two of the three
desalination plants in Gaza

00:02:06.090 --> 00:02:07.473
had to shut down.

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:11.610
The last desalination plant
that's still in operation

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:15.333
was only working at 5%
capacity in late October.

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:18.540
All wastewater plants in Gaza

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:21.300
are shut down due to the lack of power,

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:24.237
resulting in raw sewage
flooding the streets.

00:02:24.237 --> 00:02:25.410
(baby crying)

00:02:25.410 --> 00:02:28.440
Since mid-October, more than 30,000 cases

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:32.103
of diarrhea have been
reported according to the WHO.

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:37.110
Over half of those are among
children under five years old.

00:02:37.110 --> 00:02:40.590
The UN's Children's Agency
warns that in conflicts areas,

00:02:40.590 --> 00:02:44.010
children under five are
20 times more likely

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:47.848
to die of diseases linked to
diarrhea than to violence.

00:02:47.848 --> 00:02:52.015
(Rafif speaking foreign language)

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:02.640
- [Narrator] Long cues of people
waiting to fill Jerry cans

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:05.250
are now commonplace across the territory

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:08.550
as water becomes increasingly scarce.

00:03:08.550 --> 00:03:11.370
The amount of water on
which Gazans rely on now

00:03:11.370 --> 00:03:14.610
is a fraction of the WHO recommended range

00:03:14.610 --> 00:03:17.403
of 50 to 100 liters a day.

00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:20.162
And it's negligible compared

00:03:20.162 --> 00:03:22.380
to what people in Israel consume

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:25.953
on average every day
according to a UN report.

00:03:27.072 --> 00:03:31.239
(Magda speaking foreign language)

00:03:33.990 --> 00:03:35.730
- [Narrator] The Israeli
military said Gaza

00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:38.220
has sufficient water supplies,

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:41.460
as well as access to
solar power and diesel.

00:03:41.460 --> 00:03:44.490
It accused Hamas of
limiting civilians' access

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:46.830
to those vital resources.

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:48.483
Hamas denies this.

00:03:49.710 --> 00:03:51.600
What Gaza really needs according

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:56.283
to humanitarian organizations
is fuel to restore power.

00:03:57.240 --> 00:04:00.090
Since the conflicts began on October 7,

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:02.880
Israel allowed only half a tanker of fuel

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:04.800
to enter the besieged enclave

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:07.349
via the Rafah border crossing with Egypt.

00:04:07.349 --> 00:04:10.783
- Fuel here in Gaza is absolutely.

00:04:10.783 --> 00:04:14.960
Everything was without fuel,
we do not have generator,

00:04:14.960 --> 00:04:17.160
we do not have functioning bakery,

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:20.527
we do not have a functioning hospital,

00:04:20.527 --> 00:04:24.226
and you cannot pump water.

00:04:24.226 --> 00:04:28.980
- [Narrator] In mid-November,
the UN said 200,000 Gazans

00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:31.200
lost access to clean water

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:35.250
after its two water distribution
contractors stop working

00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:36.537
due to the lack of fuel.

00:04:36.537 --> 00:04:37.890
(truck horn beeping)

00:04:37.890 --> 00:04:41.400
Some aid trucks have entered
Gaza in recent weeks,

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:42.570
but the UN says

00:04:42.570 --> 00:04:45.604
they are not bringing in
nearly enough fresh water.

00:04:45.604 --> 00:04:48.604
(suspenseful music)

